case1.rea
-3                      spatial dimension  ( < 0 --> generate .rea/.re2 pair)
1                       number of fields
#=======================================================================
#
#  term_demo_case1 -- Shaver et al. (Trans. ANS 116, 2017) first test case.
#  "1D via 2D rectangular mesh": inlet/outlet normal to the flow (x), SYM on
#  the two long sides (y), single periodic layer (z) to keep it a thin 3D
#  box standing in for a 2D case. Nondimensional domain length = 1 (paper's
#  z-coordinate maps to this mesh's x).
#
#  IN/OUT (not "E") for west/east: a literal "E" is genbox's own default for
#  every ORDINARY interior element face too (any non-edge element's west face
#  is unconditionally written as "E", identical to a true boundary "E"), so
#  usrdat2 cannot tell a real exposed boundary from an interior face by string
#  match alone when both say "E". Giving the real boundary a distinct code
#  (like SYM/W already do) is what makes case1.usr's cbc-string match in
#  usrdat2 actually work.
#
#=======================================================================
#
Box
-20  -1  -1                                           nelx,nely,nelz for Box
0  1  1.                                              x0,x1,gain
0  0.1  1.                                             y0,y1,gain
0  0.1  1.                                             z0,z1,gain
v  ,O  ,SYM,SYM,E  ,E                                  bc's (3 chars each!)
